From 3f7cd5dc2ba3c24cd9f5a36ba96f8843f9d799f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abhishek <abhishek01789@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 21:39:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 24/40] Alt+Tab: port GNOME's Coverflow Alt-Tab switcher

The selected window faces you in the centre. The others turn 90 degrees
and stack to the left and right, as in dsheeler/CoverflowAltTab with its
default settings. Past the last window the stack flips back to the first.
The opening, closing, backdrop and white glow stay the shared ones.

The switcher core takes a camera field of view per layout (Coverflow uses
Clutter's 60 degrees) and a debugKey hook, and index.tsx gets a
debug.windowSwitcher IPC method. Flip 3D stays available.
